<mxCell id="b99" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;spacingTop=4;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;spacingTop=2;" value="Legend / rules of thumb" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1660" y="100" width="300" height="1060" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="t100" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Colours&lt;br&gt;blue = people and access&lt;br&gt;green = customer / tenant shape&lt;br&gt;yellow = data plumbing (needs care)&lt;br&gt;red = affects every user&lt;br&gt;grey = read-only&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Golden rules&lt;br&gt;1. Every write goes to NexoraDB; no admin page touches Octo or customer DBs.&lt;br&gt;2. Nothing needs a restart except a new row in /admin/clients.&lt;br&gt;3. Permission changes: &amp;lt;= 30 s. Branding / process / tenant registries: &amp;lt;= 60 s.&lt;br&gt;4. Deny override is the only &#x27;no&#x27; in the system.&lt;br&gt;5. Secrets never go through the UI - env files on the server only.&lt;br&gt;6. Schema changes are never done in the UI: sql/_migrations + push to main.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Where to read more&lt;br&gt;docs/design/permissions.md&lt;br&gt;docs/howto/white-label.md&lt;br&gt;docs/design/architecture-conventions.md" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1672" y="130" width="280" height="1000" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="2 Onboarding a customer - step flow" id="2_Onboarding_a_customer_-_step_flow"><mxGraphModel dx="1200" dy="700" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2000" pageHeight="900" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="t1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=20;whiteSpace=wrap;fontStyle=1;" value="Onboarding a new customer - which admin page, in which order" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1400" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
